      239.47,
      278.83,
      359.48,
      287.9
    ],
    "text": "STATEMENT OF LEGAL EFFECT",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Italic"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      8.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 1,
    "bbox": [
      143.47,
      298.15,
      455.51,
      326.42
    ],
    "text": "Clause 2 : This clause amends section 2 of the Prevention of Frauds Ordinance(Chapter 70) (hereinafter referred to as the \u201cprincipal enactment\u201d) and the legal effect ofthe section is to set out new requirements for signing a deed or instrument.",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Italic",
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      8.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 1,
    "bbox": [
      143.47,
      336.55,
      455.54,
      355.22
    ],
    "text": "Clause 3 : This clause amends section 4 of the principal enactment and the legal effectof the section is to set out new requirements for signing a will, testament or codicil.",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Italic",
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      8.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 1,
    "bbox": [
      155.47,
      365.35,
      424.08,
      374.42
    ],
    "text": "Clause 4 : This clause is consequential to the amendment made by Clause 3.",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Italic",
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      8.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 1,
    "bbox": [
      143.47,
      384.55,
      455.41,
      403.22
    ],
    "text": "Clause 5 : This clause amends section 16 of the principal enactment and the legal effectof the section is to make provision for deeds to be executed in triplicate.",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Italic",
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      8.0
    ]
  },
